---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const updated = "6 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms - Hermes"
  description="The terms that apply to Hermes clinics, staff and patients."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-strong">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink">Terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">What Hermes is</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Hermes is care-loop software that helps a clinic receive laboratory
          results, triage them by severity, notify the patient and track the case
          until a clinician signs it off. It is provided to clinics; individual
          patients use it through their clinic.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">
          Not a diagnosis and not for emergencies
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          A screening flag is not a diagnosis. The plain-language summary is
          generated from the laboratory value and does not replace clinical
          judgment. If you feel unwell or think you are having an emergency,
          contact emergency services or your clinic directly; do not wait for an
          app notification.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Accounts</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Staff accounts are created by an administrator invite and are personal.
          Do not share a password or session. Patients sign in with a one-time
          code sent to the phone number their clinic holds. Tell your clinic
          immediately if your number changes or you think someone else has
          accessed your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Do not attempt to access another patient's record, probe the service
          for vulnerabilities without written permission, submit false
          laboratory data, or use Hermes to send unlawful or abusive content.
          Clinic staff must act within their role and assigned clinic.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">
          Clinical responsibility
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The treating clinic remains responsible for clinical decisions,
          consent, record keeping and follow-up. Hermes provides the workflow,
          the clock and the audit trail; it does not choose a treatment plan.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We aim to keep the service available and to deliver notifications
          promptly, but delivery can depend on mobile networks and SMS or push
          providers. Planned maintenance is communicated to clinics in advance.
          Notification failure does not remove the clinic's duty to follow up.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the extent permitted by law, Hermes is not liable for indirect or
          consequential loss, or for clinical decisions made by a clinic. Nothing
          in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited,
          including for death or personal injury caused by negligence.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms are governed by the laws of Kenya. Disputes are subject to
          the exclusive jurisdiction of the Kenyan courts, unless your clinic's
          contract says otherwise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update these terms as the service changes. The date above shows
          the current version; continued use after an update means you accept it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
